# Allocations from docs/design/primitives/flex.md, at 80 columns. A bar is wider than any
# allocation, so the origin of a child shows the cells the children before it were given.
# `length(4) fill(1) max(4)` gives 4, 70 (what 80 columns leave after 4, 4, and two spacing cells),
# and 4. The percentages are floors of 79, the cells left after one spacing cell: 19 and 59. The
# ratio is a third of 79 rounded down, 26. Two equal fills over short children split the 77 cells
# left after their own two into 39 and 38 extra, the earlier child keeping the odd cell. `w`
# changes the fill weights, `s` the spacing.
app flex
size desktop

expect node type=Flex nth=0 frame 0,3,80x1
expect node type=_LayoutValueModifier nth=1 frame 5,3,80x1
expect node type=_LayoutValueModifier nth=2 frame 76,3,80x1
expect node type=Flex nth=1 frame 0,5,79x1
expect node type=_LayoutValueModifier nth=4 frame 20,5,80x1
expect node type=_LayoutValueModifier nth=6 frame 27,7,80x1
expect node type=_LayoutValueModifier nth=8 frame 41,9,1x1
expect node type=_LayoutValueModifier nth=10 frame 79,11,1x1
check no-dirty-after-pass requirements-aggregate
shot desktop

# Weights 1:2 share the same 77 cells as 26 and 51 extra, the odd cell to the earlier child:
# `A` is 27 wide, so `B` starts at 28.
type "w"
expect text 8 "fill(1) fill(2)"
expect node type=_LayoutValueModifier nth=8 frame 28,9,1x1
shot weights-1-2

# Spacing 2 takes two more cells from row 1's fill: 80 - 4 - 4 - 4 = 68, and `B` starts after
# the first child's four cells and two spacing cells.
type "s"
expect node type=_LayoutValueModifier nth=1 frame 6,3,80x1
expect text 20 "spacing 2"
check no-dirty-after-pass requirements-aggregate
